TASK.r:
PHP WASM — CONFIRMED NOT WORKING. Root cause:
        1. cdn.jsdelivr.net/npm/php-wasm/php-tags.jsdelivr.mjs loads as a module script tag but does NOT expose window.__php_wasm_execute. The package expects a bundler (Vite/webpack), not a raw script tag.
        2. executePHP() falls through to phpJSFallback() which attempts a broken phpToJS() transpiler that never produces real output.
        3. runPhpSimulation() then runs — so the output LOOKS correct but it is hardcoded strings, not executed PHP.
        FIX: Replace the CDN approach with @php-wasm/web loaded via esm.sh (ESM-compatible). The correct init pattern is:
          import { PHP } from 'https://esm.sh/@php-wasm/web';
          const php = await PHP.load('8.3', { ...options });
          const result = await php.run({ code: userCode });
        This gives a real PHP runtime. Artifact will be built once approach is confirmed viable in browser context.
